The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'data-to-insights': {'ecommerce': ['classification_model_2_results', 'site_wide_promotion', 'partitions', 'rev_transactions', 'products', 'product_list', 'days_with_rain', 'checkout_nudge', 'all_sessions', 'sales_report', 'sales_by_sku', 'web_analytics', 'categories', 'all_sessions_raw', 'partition_by_day']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and why they matter  
• `channelGrouping` : the acquisition channel we need to report on (GROUP BY key).  
• `geoNetwork_country` : country we must compare inside every channel grouping.  
• `totals_transactions` : numeric field to SUM so we know “total number of transactions”.  
• `fullVisitorId / visitId` : can identify a session‑level record; useful when we “remove any duplicate records” (i.e. `SELECT DISTINCT` or use these ids in a de‑duplication step).

Typical filters / conditions  
• Remove duplicate rows first → `WITH dedup AS (SELECT DISTINCT … FROM …)`  
• Only keep channel groupings that appear in more than one country → `HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT country) > 1`  
• Pick the country with the highest transactions in each qualifying channel → window function `ROW_NUMBER()` ordered by `SUM(totals_transactions)` DESC.

Below are ten progressively richer BigQuery examples (each limited to 20 rows) that explore the dataset and culminate in the required answer.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a few rows to understand the structure
SELECT *
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct list of channel groupings
SELECT DISTINCT channelGrouping
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct list of countries that recorded at least one transaction
SELECT DISTINCT geoNetwork_country
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
WHERE totals_transactions IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Transaction totals per (channel, country) pair – duplicates removed
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT channelGrouping,
                  geoNetwork_country AS country,
                  totals_transactions
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
)
SELECT channelGrouping,
       country,
       SUM(totals_transactions) AS total_transactions
FROM dedup
GROUP BY channelGrouping, country
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count how many different countries occur in each channel grouping
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT channelGrouping,
                  geoNetwork_country AS country
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
)
SELECT channelGrouping,
       COUNT(DISTINCT country) AS country_count
FROM dedup
GROUP BY channelGrouping
HAVING country_count > 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same as #5 but keep the country list as an array for inspection
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT channelGrouping,
                  geoNetwork_country AS country
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
)
SELECT channelGrouping,
       ARRAY_AGG(country) AS country_list
FROM dedup
GROUP BY channelGrouping
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT country) > 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate transactions and keep rank of countries within each channel
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT channelGrouping,
                  geoNetwork_country AS country,
                  totals_transactions
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
),
agg AS (
  SELECT channelGrouping,
         country,
         SUM(totals_transactions) AS total_transactions
  FROM dedup
  GROUP BY channelGrouping, country
)
SELECT channelGrouping,
       country,
